<body><div class=WordSection1>
<div class="brand">📚 ENGLISH CODING · 영어코딩</div>
<h1>🖨️ Beginner 1 — print() and f-strings</h1>
<p><strong>Topic:</strong> Showing words on the screen · <strong>Course:</strong> Text Adventure (Python) · <strong>Time:</strong> about 40 minutes</p>
<p>This is your first worksheet. You do not need a computer for most of it. You read code, guess what the screen shows, and fix small mistakes on paper.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>🧠 Words to know: <strong>print</strong>, <strong>variable</strong>, <strong>f-string</strong>, <strong>quotes</strong>, <strong>output</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<pre><code class="language-python">print(&quot;Hello!&quot;)                 # screen shows:  Hello!

name = &quot;Amy&quot;
print(f&quot;Hi {name}&quot;)             # screen shows:  Hi Amy

print(&quot;Hi {name}&quot;)              # screen shows:  Hi {name}
</code></pre>
<p>The little <strong>f</strong> is what swaps the box for its value.</p>
<hr />
<h2>1 · Warm Up ⭕</h2>
<p><strong>Which line puts words on the screen? Circle one:</strong> <code>name = "Amy"</code> · <code>print("Amy")</code></p>
<p><strong>Which line makes a variable? Circle one:</strong> <code>print("hp")</code> · <code>hp = 100</code></p>
<p><strong>Which line needs an <code>f</code>? Circle one:</strong> <code>print("Hello!")</code> · <code>print("Hello {name}")</code></p>
<hr />
<h2>2 · Predict 🔮</h2>
<p>Read the code. Write exactly what the screen shows.</p>
<pre><code class="language-python">name = &quot;Warrior&quot;
health = 100
print(f&quot;{name} has {health} health&quot;)
</code></pre>
<p><strong>What appears on screen?</strong></p>
<p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p>

<pre><code class="language-python">first = &quot;Dark&quot;
second = &quot;Knight&quot;
print(first + second)
</code></pre>
<p><strong>What appears on screen? Look carefully at the spaces.</strong></p>
<p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p>

<pre><code class="language-python">damage = 20
bonus = 5
print(f&quot;Total damage: {damage + bonus}&quot;)
</code></pre>
<p><strong>What number appears?</strong></p>
<p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p>

<hr />
<h2>3 · Spot the Bug 🐛</h2>
<p>Each one is broken. Write the fixed line.</p>
<p><strong>Bug A</strong> — This should show <code>Hello, Amy!</code> but it shows <code>Hello, {name}!</code></p>
<pre><code class="language-python">name = &quot;Amy&quot;
print(&quot;Hello, {name}!&quot;)
</code></pre>
<p><strong>Write the fixed line:</strong></p>
<p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p>

<p><strong>Bug B</strong> — This should show the word <code>Sword</code> but Python gives an error.</p>
<pre><code class="language-python">print(Sword)
</code></pre>
<p><strong>Write the fixed line:</strong></p>
<p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p>

<p><strong>Bug C</strong> — This should show <code>Level 5</code> but Python gives an error.</p>
<pre><code class="language-python">level = 5
print(f&quot;Level {level}&quot;
</code></pre>
<p><strong>Write the fixed line:</strong></p>
<p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p>

<hr />
<h2>4 · Explain the Code 📖</h2>
<p>Read this small program.</p>
<pre><code class="language-python">hero = &quot;Mina&quot;
potions = 3
print(f&quot;{hero} the brave&quot;)
print(f&quot;You carry {potions} potions.&quot;)
</code></pre>
<p><strong>Which two lines make a variable? Write their names.</strong></p>
<p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p>

<p><strong>What does <code>{hero}</code> turn into on the screen?</strong></p>
<p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p>

<p><strong>How many lines appear on the screen when you run this?</strong></p>
<p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p>

<p><strong>Change <code>potions</code> to <code>7</code>. What is different on the screen?</strong></p>
<p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p>

<hr />
<h2>5 · Explain Your Lesson Code 🎥</h2>
<p>Record a short video on your phone (or a parent's phone). Show the code you wrote in your lesson and talk about it. Try to use these words: <strong>print</strong>, <strong>variable</strong>, <strong>f-string</strong>.</p>
<blockquote>
<ol>
<li>Read out one <code>print</code> line from your code.</li>
<li>Point to a <strong>variable</strong> and say its name.</li>
<li>Read an <code>f"..."</code> line and say what gets swapped in.</li>
</ol>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<h3>Submit ✅</h3>
<p>Send a photo of this worksheet and your video to teacher on KakaoTalk.</p>
